                         Password Script

       This TELIX SALT script allows you to select different 
       passwords for each BBS you call without having to remember
       the password or look it up each time you call.

       The script takes the password it finds in the active TELIX 
       Phone Directory under the number you dialed, adds a 
       carriage return, and enters it as a macro in function key 
       3.  If you enter your first name followed by a carriage 
       return in FK1, your second name plus a carriage return in 
       FK2 you can answer the common log-on prompts by hitting FK1
       then FK2 then FK3.  You don't have to write a log-on 
       script for each BBS.

       The files are as follows:

       READ.ME         This file
       PASSING.SLT     The source file - very simple
       PASSING.SLC     The script file (Object)

       Make sure you enter a password in the directory for each 
       BBS you call and that the script for all BBSs is PASSING.  
       There should be no macro defined for FK3 in the terminal 
       or user key tables or they will override the script loaded 
       macro. Also make sure that the file PASSING.SLC is in the 
       same directory as TELIX.EXE 

       Herb Lavanhar
